title: snes-pilotwings-nochip
message: >-
  If you use this work, or the measurements it publishes, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gustavo
    family-names: Franco
    alias: gufranco
repository-code: https://github.com/gufranco/snes-pilotwings-nochip
url: https://github.com/gufranco/snes-pilotwings-nochip
abstract: >-
  Removes the DSP-1 from Pilotwings for the Super Nintendo, in all three of its
  regional releases, by replacing what the coprocessor computed with tables and
  65816 routines that run on the console itself. The retail cartridges are the
  only authority on what the game asks, and the part's own microcode is the only
  authority on what the answer is. Publishes the measurement that decides which
  commands can be tabulated and which must be computed.
keywords:
  - super-nintendo
  - pilotwings
  - dsp1
  - upd7725
  - rom-hacking
  - 65816
  - conformance
